NODE id=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/settle.Worker.SettleWithdrawals kind=method
  digest=b3:926380511d646192f4bca2f5b71c72ca1bb5935a02c64e3c80078b2cbdab1ff2 file=layerx/internal/settle/settle.go range=315:372 lang=go exported=true byte_range=11674:14055
  sig=func (w *Worker) SettleWithdrawals(ctx context.Context) (string, error)
  doc=SettleWithdrawals pays out queued withdrawals as real USDL on Paxeer: it\nseals the payable set under a deterministic payout root (freezing the\nrecipients), submits the operator-signed vault payout, and marks each\nwithdrawal settled with the on-chain tx — only after it confirms. Returns the\npayout root (empty when there was nothing payable). Idempotent + crash-safe:\nthe frozen root makes the on-chain batch id stable, so a retried submit never\ndouble-pays. Withdrawals whose DID has no mapped EVM address are skipped (left\nqueued) until a binding exists. Safe to call concurrently; serialized.
EDGES
  ^contains=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/settle.Worker
  ^defines=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/settle/settle.go

